---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { lineup, mixTimeClaim } from '../data/models';
import ApplicationsGrid from '../components/ApplicationsGrid.astro';
import WhatsAppLink from '../components/WhatsAppLink.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="On-site concrete for rapid-set, latex-modified, and shotcrete work | Equip Solutions Group"
  description="Independent StarMix representative for on-site concrete. Rapid-set, latex-modified overlay, and shotcrete work that a rotating drum cannot hold. Equipment and parts sourcing as a secondary desk.">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Independent representative</p>
      <h1>A rotating drum cannot hold the mix this job needs.</h1>
      <p>Rapid-set starts hydrating in the barrel. Latex-modified overlay has a short working window and a ratio you meter, not guess. Shotcrete has to match the nozzle, not the truckload. Mix on site, on demand, at the ratio the pour calls for &mdash; with nothing returned.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Request a Quote</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="strip">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="strip-grid">
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">{lineup.largestBinYd3}<span>yd&sup3;</span></div>
          <div class="strip-label">Largest published bin</div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">{lineup.peakProductionYd3Hr}<span>yd&sup3;/hr</span></div>
          <div class="strip-label">Peak line production</div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">{mixTimeClaim.figure}<span>{mixTimeClaim.unit}</span></div>
          <div class="strip-label">{mixTimeClaim.label}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">{lineup.modelCount}</div>
          <div class="strip-label">Models, {lineup.seriesCount} series</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="applications">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Applications</p>
        <h2>Jobs a rotating drum cannot do cleanly</h2>
        <p class="lede">Bridge decks, night lane-returns, shotcrete, scattered municipal pours, remote sites, and work too small to justify a barrel load. Each is a different buyer with a different constraint.</p>
      </div>
      <ApplicationsGrid />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">StarMix</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">The line I represent</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">StarMix plants carry sand, stone, cement, water and admixture dry, and mix at the discharge. That is how a night lane-return, a latex-modified overlay, or a shotcrete crew gets the ratio the job called for &mdash; without a returned load.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--graphite);">Six models across three series. Specs are manufacturer-published and confirmed on the written quote. Se habla espa&ntilde;ol.</p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/starmix/">See the StarMix line</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ph ph--tall">Photo &mdash; volumetric plant discharging on site<br>Recommended 900&times;1200</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split split--narrow">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">After the sale</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">Parts and support</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="lede">Genuine SMI components, operator training, and a parts desk that still answers when the unit is two years in. Calibration and mix design are what stand between a good pour and a rejected one &mdash; that is the support, not a ticket queue.</p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/parts/#starmix">SMI parts</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/parts/#request">Request a part</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Also</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-2);text-transform:uppercase;">Equipment and parts sourcing</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">A secondary desk for used units, surplus machines, and numbers the counter has already given up on. Not a second manufacturer line &mdash; one person who will make the calls when the catalog ends.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:1.25rem;"><a class="card-link" href="/sourcing/">How sourcing works</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Tell me the pour, not the model number"
    body="Application, typical load, and when you need to be placing. I will come back with a real spec and a real number.">
    <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Request a Quote</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
    <p class="cta-alt" slot="under">
      <WhatsAppLink />
      <span class="spanish-note">Se habla espa&ntilde;ol. Sales, training, and support in Spanish.</span>
    </p>
  </CtaBand>

</BaseLayout>
